# Next.js engineering anchor

**Only apply** when the active frontend package declares next. Do not impose Next.js patterns on SvelteKit or a non-Next React project.

Before a material change, audit or fix, run:
node "$CURSOR_DEV_TOOLKIT_ROOT/scripts/frontend-preflight.mjs" --root "$FRONTEND_ROOT" --framework nextjs

Requires tested Next.js 16.4.0 with App Router and compatible Node/TS/React baseline. On failure STOP and explicitly ask permission for a controlled upgrade/migration; never install/codemod automatically.

On PASS, read relevant Contents sections:
$CURSOR_DEV_TOOLKIT_ROOT/skills/engineering/_standards/nextjs-engineering-standard.md
plus the shared Frontend Core.

Hard invariants: default Server Components, narrow use client boundary, server-side authorization on each Server Function, direct server data access rather than self HTTP, version-aware Cache Components with user scope. Inspect next.config first; do not silently enable cacheComponents on existing apps.

Explicit workflows: /nextjs-engineering-audit and /nextjs-engineering-fix.
